# DEC-140 counted a subclass's own method for a call typed as its ancestor,
# but not a module a subclass mixes in: `item.label` with `item` a `Base`
# may be a `Child`, whose `include Auditing` puts `Auditing#label` ahead of
# `Base#label`, and it was excluded as `different_owner` (`trail`, which
# `Base` lacks, as `no_such_method`). Both are possible now. `Base.new` is
# exactly a `Base`, and `Other` reaches `Auditing` through a module but is
# no subclass of `Base`, so those stay as they were.
refs Auditing#label confirmed=1 possible=1 excluded=1
refs Auditing#trail confirmed=0 possible=1 excluded=0
refs Base#label confirmed=2 possible=0
dead app.rb Auditing#trail=single-caller
